-- title:
--   Kernel of an abelian-quotient family equals the toric points
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $(N_0,p,A)$, that is: a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation of $\mathbb Q$ at $p$ restricting to the generic point along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, a scheme $X$ with a structure morphism $f$ to that base carrying a relative group law, a bijection $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbb Q}) =$ `JZero N₀` onto the generic-fibre points of $f$, and a bijection $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from `JZeroC (ResidueField A) N₀` onto the points of $f$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field of $A$; assume `Λ.IsJacobian`, i.e. $f$ satisfies the abelian-scheme property bundle, its group law is commutative, $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ and $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ are additive, $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$ is Galois-equivariant, reduction of points agrees with `reductionModL` whenever the reduction inputs hold, and every Hecke operator is induced by an endomorphism of $f$. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, i.e. a smooth, separated, surjective group object $g \colon G \to$ base with commutative relative group law, preconnected fibres, a Galois- and Hecke-compatible additive bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ from `JZero (N₀ * p)` onto the generic points of $g$, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, proper generic fibre, a toric rank with its toric lift and the two special-fibre abelian-quotient morphisms $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,i$. Suppose given, for every $m$ coprime to $p$, an additive map $\mathrm{abq}_m$ from $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ — the subgroup of `JZero (N₀ * p)` generated by the $m$-torsion points whose associated generic point of $g$ extends to an $A$-point over $\sigma_A$ — to $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbb Q})^2$, such that each value is killed by $m$, and such that whenever $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ and $s$ is an $A$-point of $g$ over $\sigma_A$ with $O.\mathrm{pts}(x)$ obtained from $s$ by pullback along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, the two components of $\mathrm{abq}_m(x)$ have `reductionModL` equal to $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1}$ of the image of the residue-field specialisation of $s$ under $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,0$, respectively $O.\mathrm{abqFibre}\,1$. Then for every $m$ coprime to $p$ and every $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ one has $\mathrm{abq}_m(x) = 0$ if and only if $x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m\,\chi$ (and the trivial subgroup if $m = 0$).
--
--   This identifies, for the Néron object attached to $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$, the kernel of the pair of abelian-quotient maps on prime-to-$p$ torsion that extends to $A$ with the toric subgroup, the characterisation of the toric part used in Ribet's level-lowering argument at $p$. It is stated for an arbitrary family of additive maps satisfying the reduction formula, and is cited when such a family is constructed (`exists_abq_family_of_coprime`) and when its image is computed (`range_abq_eq_torsionBy_of_forall_reductionModL_eq`).
